# G109 — TV Show Tracker

*v2. See `tv-tracker.md` for prose: library vs watchlist split,
hierarchical progress roll-up from leaf flags, next-up as
first-unwatched-in-order, airing-since as caller-cutoff filter.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault TV Dashboard

[vault-tv-dashboard @user-id
    IN ORDER TO
        render a Continue Watching row from the user's watchlist
        joined against the canonical library
        and a New Episodes row filtered by the user's last visit

    @lib <- [tv[library-load {path: "tv/library.json"}]]
    @wl  <- [tv[watchlist-load {path: "tv/" + @user-id + ".json"}]]
    @last-open <- [user[last-dashboard-open-ms {id: @user-id}]]

    @continuing <- [tv[currently-watching
                        {library: @lib, watchlist: @wl}]]

    [ui[render-row
        {title: "Continue Watching",
         items: @continuing mapped to ({
            show: @show,
            next-up:  [tv[next-up       {show: @show, watchlist: @wl}]],
            progress: [tv[show-progress {show: @show, watchlist: @wl}]]
         })}]]

    @new <- [tv[library-airing-since
                  {library: @lib, since-ms: @last-open}]]
    [ui[render-row {title: "New Episodes", items: @new}]]

    sync @user-events {
        mark-watched @show-id @season @episode ->
            [tv[watchlist-mark-watched
                  {watchlist: @wl, show-id: @show-id,
                   season: @season, episode: @episode}]]
            [tv[watchlist-save
                  {watchlist: @wl,
                   path: "tv/" + @user-id + ".json"}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[tv
    library
    library-add-show          {library, show}
    library-add-episode       {library, episode}           ;; || unknown-show
    library-airing-since      {library, since-ms}
    watchlist
    watchlist-load            {path}
    watchlist-save            {watchlist, path}
    watchlist-mark-watched    {watchlist, show-id, season, episode}
    watchlist-is-watched      {watchlist, show-id, season, episode}
    show-progress             {show, watchlist}
    next-up                   {show, watchlist}            ;; -> Episode | none
    currently-watching        {library, watchlist}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: library and watchlist as separate contexts

[tv[library[...]]]      ;; canonical, shared across users
[tv[watchlist[...]]]    ;; per-user, private

The two bracket contexts share the `episode-key` join type but never
merge state. A user switching accounts swaps the inner watchlist while
leaving the library untouched. Conflating them — the v1 temptation —
would fork canonical data per user.

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: next-up as `where` over sorted episodes

[tv[next-up {show: @s, watchlist: @wl}]
    IN ORDER TO
        return the first episode the user has not yet watched
        when walking (season, episode) in natural order

    @s:episodes
        ordered by season ascending, episode ascending
        where [tv[watchlist-is-watched
                    {watchlist: @wl, show-id: @s:id,
                     season: @episode:season,
                     episode: @episode:episode}]] is false
        first
        || -> none
]

Out-of-order viewing returns the earliest gap. A fully-watched show
resists the first-match and surfaces `none`, which the UI renders as
a "Watched" badge rather than a "Resume" button.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: currently-watching as a `where` range

[tv[currently-watching {library: @lib, watchlist: @wl}]
    @lib:shows
        where watched-count is greater than zero
        and watched-count is less than total-episode-count
]

Started-but-not-finished is a bounded interval on a derived quantity.
Zero is candidacy; equal is completion; anything strictly between is
the "in the middle" row the UI wants.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @lib <- [tv[library]]
    @bb  <- {id: 1, title: "Breaking Bad", episodes: [
                {season: 1, episode: 1, title: "Pilot",
                 duration-min: 47, aired-ms: 1000000}
                {season: 1, episode: 2, title: "Cat's in the Bag",
                 duration-min: 48, aired-ms: 1600000}
                {season: 1, episode: 3, title: "Bag's in the River",
                 duration-min: 47, aired-ms: 2200000}
            ]}
    [tv[library-add-show {library: @lib, show: @bb}]]

    @wl <- [tv[watchlist]]
    [tv[watchlist-mark-watched
          {watchlist: @wl, show-id: 1, season: 1, episode: 1}]]
    [tv[watchlist-mark-watched
          {watchlist: @wl, show-id: 1, season: 1, episode: 2}]]

    -> [tv[next-up {show: @bb, watchlist: @wl}]]
    ;; -> Episode S1E3

    -> [tv[show-progress {show: @bb, watchlist: @wl}]]
    ;; -> {watched: 2, total: 3, percent: 66}
]
